

(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "//go:build linux"] [19 1 "// posix's process and file functions (PY6e; Modules/posixmodule.c): stat_result with its float and nanosecond"] [20 1 "// times, scandir and DirEntry, the descriptors' functions (dup2, pread, readv, inheritable and blocking flags),"] [21 1 "// the processes' (waitpid, wait3, wait4, execv, execve, system, times, uname), sysconf, confstr and pathconf over"] [22 1 "// musl's tables, statvfs, the terminal's few (isatty from the device's major number). posix has no fork: Go's"] [23 1 "// runtime is multithreaded, so pyi starts children only through _posixsubprocess.fork_exec (Go's ForkExec), and"] [24 1 "// test.support's has_fork_support is False (the class no-fork)."] [46 2 "// stat_result(seq) of ten: its float times from the int slots (statresult_new)"] [75 1 "// fildesFns are the functions whose descriptor is fildes_converter's (a negative one a ValueError); the others take"] [76 1 "// `int fd` (queue 249)."] [79 1 "// fdArg is a file descriptor argument: an int, or an object's fileno()."] [121 1 "// isattyFd is isatty(3) without its ioctl: a character device of a terminal's major number (tty, console, pts)."] [122 1 "// isattyFd is musl's isatty: TIOCGWINSZ succeeds (queue 220: the ioctl's struct by its address, termios'; before, the"] [123 1 "// device's major number, which missed a pty's master)."] [130 1 "// pathOrFd is a path argument that may also be a descriptor (os.stat(fd)): path_converter with allow_fd, a bool a"] [131 1 "// descriptor after a RuntimeWarning as _fd_converter warns."] [153 1 "// posixWarnHook is warnings.warn(msg, category), set by makePosix for the converters' warnings."] [156 1 "// fdConv is _fd_converter: an int (a bool warns first) within C's int."] [177 1 "// isBytesPath is a path argument that is bytes, or os.PathLike of bytes: the results are bytes then."] [193 1 "// nameDecode is os.fsdecode of a name: UTF-8, an undecodable byte a surrogate (surrogateescape)."] [212 1 "// fildesWarns are the functions whose descriptor is CPython's fildes converter, which warns of a bool."] [215 1 "// fdDir marks listdir's and scandir's directory given as a descriptor."] [218 1 "// atFdCwd is AT_FDCWD, dir_fd's default."] [221 1 "// dirFd is a dir_fd argument by its keyword (dir_fd_converter): absent or None the current directory, else a"] [222 1 "// descriptor."] [234 1 "// atPath is the *at functions' path: p relative to the directory dirfd as a path the plain calls take, an"] [235 1 "// absolute path or one of the current directory unchanged, else /proc/self/fd/DIRFD/p, the descriptor checked"] [236 1 "// first so that a bad one is EBADF and a file's ENOTDIR, as openat(2) answers (Go's syscall has no linkat,"] [237 1 "// readlinkat, symlinkat or flags for unlinkat; every *at goes this one way)."] [255 1 "// noFollowPath is a path naming the symbolic link p itself, for the calls that have no l* form in Go's syscall"] [256 1 "// (utimensat's AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW): /proc/self/fd/N of an O_PATH|O_NOFOLLOW descriptor, closed by done."] [265 24 "// O_PATH, the same on amd64 and arm64"] [267 1 "// atArgs are a path function's dir_fd and follow_symlinks checked as CPython checks them: fd with dir_fd or"] [268 1 "// follow_symlinks=False is a ValueError."] [297 1 "// splitKw is a call's positional arguments and its keyword ones by name."] [337 2 "// CPython's on musl Linux but those of functions pyi lacks (ptsname_r):"] [338 2 "// the *at functions through atPath, futimens and lutimes through /proc/self/fd"] [369 5 "// CPython's `int fd` (not _PyLong_FileDescriptor_Converter): a negative descriptor reaches the system"] [370 5 "// call, OSError EBADF (queue 249: asyncio's _sock_sendfile_native reads os.fstat(-1)'s OSError as"] [371 5 "// \"not a regular file\")"] [397 2 "// ---- stat"] [414 37 "// lstat takes no descriptor"] [486 19 "// AT_EACCESS"] [489 19 "// AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW"] [579 4 "// fchmodat(AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW) as musl answers it: a link's mode cannot change (EOPNOTSUPP, which"] [580 4 "// os_chmod_impl turns into NotImplementedError), anything else's does"] [716 5 "// linkat(AT_SYMLINK_FOLLOW) by default: the link's target linked, not the link"] [786 44 "// futimens(fd)"] [872 27 "// NODEV"] [889 28 "// makedev(NODEV, NODEV)"] [949 2 "// ---- listdir, scandir"] [963 4 "// fdopendir(dup(fd)) as a fresh open of the descriptor's directory, its entries' paths their names"] [1046 2 "// ---- descriptors"] [1209 3 "// no TIOCGWINSZ without unsafe: the size the environment gives, else 80x24"] [1329 3 "// the GIL released while it blocks, as posixmodule.c's Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS (PY7: a blocking socket's sendfile"] [1330 3 "// held it, so the thread reading the other end never ran: test_socket's SendfileUsingSendfileTest.testOffset)"] [1352 2 "// ---- processes"] [1457 37 "// the kernel's 40..1, as libc's -20..19"] [1506 73 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [1599 45 "// fexecve"] [1659 2 "// ---- configuration"] [1748 1 "// sysconfDynamic is musl's sysconf of the values it computes (src/conf/sysconf.c)."] [1767 10 "// SC_ARG_MAX"] [1772 10 "// SC_CHILD_MAX"] [1774 10 "// SC_OPEN_MAX"] [1776 11 "// SC_PAGESIZE (SC_PAGE_SIZE)"] [1778 15 "// SC_NPROCESSORS_CONF, SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN"] [1780 11 "// SC_PHYS_PAGES"] [1783 11 "// SC_AVPHYS_PAGES"] [1786 12 "// SC_MINSIGSTKSZ: the auxiliary vector's AT_MINSIGSTKSZ, at least MINSIGSTKSZ"] [1814 1 "// ---- DirEntry and scandir's iterator"] [1819 25 "// d_type's bits"] [1820 25 "// d_ino"] [1824 1 "// dirent is one linux_dirent64 of getdents64."] [1831 1 "// readDirents is readdir(3) over getdents64: each entry's name, d_ino and d_type, \".\" and \"..\" left out."] [1863 1 "// mode is d_type as os.FileMode's type bits; DT_UNKNOWN an lstat of the entry, as Go's ReadDir does."] [1897 1 "// scandirFinalize is ScandirIterator_finalize (queue 241): an iterator not closed (nor exhausted) warns"] [1898 1 "// ResourceWarning \"unclosed scandir iterator %R\" (its source the iterator) and is closed."] [2043 1 "// openDir is opendir(3): the path opened O_DIRECTORY, so a FIFO or a file fails at once (os.Open of a FIFO blocks"] [2044 1 "// until a writer opens it: os.walk of a named pipe hung)."] [2053 1 "// posixMinArgs are the positional arguments posix's functions need (Argument Clinic's required ones), so that a"] [2054 1 "// short call is a TypeError, never an index past args (a Go panic ended test_os's driver in test_readinto_badarg)."] [2066 1 "// posixMaxArgs are the arguments of posix's functions that take a fixed few: none for the no-argument functions"] [2067 1 "// (testNoArgFunctions), more a TypeError."] [2093 1 "// devConv is a dev_t argument (_Py_Dev_Converter): an int of 64 bits, -1 NODEV; max the bound of major's and"] [2094 1 "// minor's unsigned int when not 0."] [2116 1 "// The system interface where TamaGo's syscall lacks it (queue 214: pyi's runtime listed in goi's table, checked in its"] [2117 1 "// tamago configurations too; builtins_os_other.go there): Linux's."] [2123 1 "// oNofollow is O_NOFOLLOW, the architecture's (a function: the constant's value differs between amd64 and arm64)."] [2128 1 "// ignorePipeSignals ignores SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ, as CPython's startup does."]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[48 13] [48 21] [81 22] [91 45] [95 23] [107 24] [133 22] [140 48] [141 24] [158 27] [159 83] [179 24] [186 48] [228 22] [243 37] [281 34] [363 35] [364 85] [368 30] [389 32] [404 25] [424 31] [450 35] [461 20] [503 25] [517 30] [525 24] [553 20] [575 29] [582 35] [627 31] [660 21] [664 40] [698 37] [702 41] [705 41] [708 31] [712 30] [729 21] [768 24] [771 25] [788 36] [791 36] [887 29] [888 30] [925 37] [945 76] [965 36] [972 53] [1073 30] [1078 49] [1087 38] [1105 15] [1105 24] [1112 51] [1123 36] [1175 35] [1203 35] [1346 28] [1405 30] [1436 13] [1436 34] [1443 86] [1484 60] [1616 35] [1664 23] [1672 23] [1685 32] [1688 31] [1698 32] [1725 35] [1